 "description": "Posts in your workspaces, newest first, one page at a time, each with the state of every destination it was sent to and the numbers it has earned so far. Call it to find one post (post_id), to check whether something published, and before changing or cancelling anything \u2014 posts_save takes a post_id from here.\n\nNumbers are as of the last sweep, and every destination carries the time it was measured \u2014 one nobody has measured yet has no metrics at all rather than zeroes.\n\n`trial` names an Instagram trial reel's graduation strategy, and is null for anything that is not one. A trial is shown to non-followers first, so its numbers come from a colder audience than an ordinary post's: compare trials with trials.\n\nEach row also carries `insights`: what the platform's own analytics said on that delivery, never summed across deliveries. reach (distinct accounts), totalWatchMs and avgWatchMs, replays, follows (gained from the post), completionRate and skipRate as fractions 0..1, `retention` \u2014 the full audience-retention curve as Facebook sends it, `points[i]` being the share still watching at i twentieths of the video and `bucketMs` one twentieth in milliseconds \u2014 and `breakdowns` such as clicks by type. retentionAt3s and retentionAtHalf are read off that curve, interpolated between buckets, so hooks can be ranked by how many viewers they held; null without a curve or a known video length. Null means the platform does not report it; a name listed in `unavailable` means it would have and refused this time. Compare watch time across platforms as totalWatchMs / views: Facebook averages per play and Instagram per viewer, so avgWatchMs is not comparable between them.\n\nEvery filter is optional and they combine: a date range, statuses, platforms, accounts, groups and products by name, where the post came from, and a caption search. Pass nextCursor back as cursor for the next page; null means there is no more.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "properties": {
   "account_id": {
    "description": "Accounts by id, from accounts_list.",
    "items": {
     "type": "string"
    },
    "type": "array"
   },
   "by": {
    "description": "With rank_by: the running total, or how much it moved over the period. Defaults to the total. Insights rank by value only.",
    "enum": [
     "value",
     "change"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   },
   "cursor": {
    "description": "nextCursor from the previous page.",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "from": {
    "description": "ISO date or date-time. Only posts that went out, or are due to, at or after this.",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "group": {
    "description": "Groups by name, from groups_list: posts to any of their accounts.",
    "items": {
     "type": "string"
    },
    "type": "array"
   },
   "limit": {
    "description": "Posts per page. Defaults to 25.",
    "maximum": 100,
    "minimum": 1,
    "type": "integer"
   },
   "order": {
    "description": "Defaults to desc.",
    "enum": [
     "asc",
     "desc"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   },
   "period": {
    "description": "The window each figure's change is measured over. Defaults to 24h.",
    "enum": [
     "24h",
     "7d"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   },
   "platform": {
    "items": {
     "enum": [
      "tiktok",
      "instagram",
      "facebook",
      "x",
      "youtube",
      "linkedin"
     ],
     "type": "string"
    },
    "type": "array"
   },
   "post_id": {
    "description": "One post by id. The other filters are ignored.",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "product": {
    "description": "Products by name or id: posts to accounts linked to them.",
    "items": {
     "type": "string"
    },
    "type": "array"
   },
   "rank_by": {
    "description": "Rank the matching posts by one figure of their best destination instead: any counter (views, likes, \u2026) or insight (reach, avgWatchMs, completionRate, retentionAt3s, retentionAtHalf, \u2026). Answers \"which hooks held viewers\" or \"what is moving now\". Ranks up to 500 matching posts; no cursor.",
    "enum": [
     "views",
     "likes",
     "comments",
     "shares",
     "saves",
     "reach",
     "totalWatchMs",
     "avgWatchMs",
     "replays",
     "follows",
     "completionRate",
     "retentionAt3s",
     "retentionAtHalf"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   },
   "search": {
    "description": "Text the caption contains, ignoring case.",
    "maxLength": 200,
    "minLength": 1,
    "type": "string"
   },
   "sort_by": {
    "description": "A counter or insight (views, likes, \u2026), \"when\", \"updated\" or \"account\". Defaults to newest first.",
    "enum": [
     "views",
     "likes",
     "comments",
     "shares",
     "saves",
     "reach",
     "totalWatchMs",
     "replays",
     "follows",
     "when",
     "updated",
     "account"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   },
   "source": {
    "description": "Where a post came from. external is one made on the platform itself and found afterwards.",
    "items": {
     "enum": [
      "web",
      "mcp",
      "api",
      "campaign",
      "external"
     ],
     "type": "string"
    },
    "type": "array"
   },
   "status": {
    "description": "published, scheduled, draft, failed or cancelled. A post matches when any of its destinations is in one of these states.",
    "items": {
     "enum": [
      "published",
      "scheduled",
      "draft",
      "failed",
      "cancelled"
     ],
     "type": "string"
    },
    "type": "array"
   },
   "to": {
    "description": "ISO date or date-time. Only posts before this.",
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "type": "object"
 },
